Screen
/ PlangOS's side of the screen. Host plang starts this (wsl … /opt/plang/plang Screen). The
/ screen is PlangOS's display: programs draw onto it, and its frames go to this app's output —
/ the pipe to host plang. Input from the host comes down on stdin, one line per event, and goes
/ to the screen. Ends when the host closes the pipe.
/ The first page is the desktop; every app opens in a window of its own.
- screen.open(ToOutput=true, OnWindow=goal.call(Name="Window")); variable.set(Name=%screen%, Value=%!data%)
- browser.start(Url="file:///home/plang/desktop.html", Screen=%screen%, OnMessage=goal.call(Name="Desktop")); variable.set(Name=%browser%, Value=%!data%)
- on input call Input
- stop %browser%

Input
- send %!data% to %screen%

Desktop
/ The desktop page asks: {"open": url} opens a window; {"window": "focus|minimize|…", "id"}
/ goes to the screen; {"files"} shows the desktop's files; {"edit": path} opens one in Writer.
/ Writer asks: {"save": path, "text"}; "from" is the window that asked.
- set %asked% to %!data%
- if %asked.open%, call Open
- if %asked.window%, call Command
- if %asked.files%, call Files
- if %asked.edit%, call Edit
- if %asked.save%, call Save

Open
- open window %asked.open% in %browser%

Command
- send %asked% to %screen%

Files
/ the desktop's files: what is in Desktop/, shown as icons
- list files in 'Desktop', write to %files%
- call ShowFiles files=%files% in %browser.desktop%

Edit
/ a file opens in Writer, in a window of its own: what it holds — a text file its text, a json file
/ its value
- open window 'file:///home/plang/app/writer/start.html' in %browser%, write to %writer%
- read %asked.edit%, write to %content%
- call Show file=%asked.edit%, content=%content% in %writer%

Save
/ Ctrl+S in Writer: the file's format writes what Writer sends — a text file's text, a json file's value
- save %asked.content% to %asked.save%
- window.callGoal(Name="Saved", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%)

Window
/ The screen says what happened to a window: the desktop's taskbar shows it. Enter in a
/ window's address field ({"navigate": what was typed, "id"}) sends that window there; its
/ menu's New window, and links opened as tabs ({"open": url}), open a window.
- set %event% to %!data%
- post %event% to %browser.desktop%
- if %event.navigate%, call Navigate
- if %event.open%, call OpenPage

Navigate
- navigate window %event.id% to %event.navigate% in %browser%

OpenPage
- open window %event.open% in %browser%
